course: dictionary
lesson: 16159
title: Withholding
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Withholding means keeping something back and not giving it, when people expected you to give it. «The school is withholding the results until next week.» The results were expected, but the school is keeping them back, so withholding means holding something back.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «He refused to answer and was withholding the truth from his mum.» Refused and not telling the truth are clues that he is keeping something back on purpose. Try your meaning in the sentence: "keeping the truth back" still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Withholding can also be about money. «Mum is withholding my pocket money because I forgot to tidy my room.» Here it is a punishment: the money is kept back. In some countries, such as the US, withholding is also tax taken from your pay before you get it.
fact: Withholding means keeping something back and not giving it when it was expected.
fact: «Withholding information» means not sharing facts that people want to know.
fact: «Withholding payment» means not paying money that is owed or expected.
fact: In some countries, especially the US, «withholding» is tax taken from your pay before you receive it.
fact: Withhold, withholds, withheld and withholding are all forms of the same word.
exercise: «The shop is withholding the refund until the broken toy comes back.» What does withholding mean here? | Giving the money away to charity | Counting the money twice | Spending the money quickly | *Keeping the money back and not giving it yet
exercise: Which of these is another form of the word withhold? | wander | *withheld | whistle | wobble
exercise: In a police show, the detective says, «The witness is withholding evidence.» What does this suggest? | The witness is giving all the proof to everyone | The witness has lost the proof | *The witness is keeping back important proof, which is dishonest | The witness is very tired
test: «Dad is withholding my phone until my homework is finished.» What is Dad doing? | *Keeping the phone back until the homework is done | Breaking the phone on purpose | Giving the phone to my friend | Buying a new phone
test: On a pay slip you may see «tax withheld». What does this mean? | Extra money added to your pay | *Tax taken out of your pay before you get it | Your pay has been paid in coins | Your boss is giving you a holiday
exam: The club is withholding payment from the builder until the work is finished. What does withholding payment mean? | Paying twice by mistake | *Not paying yet, keeping the money back until the work is done | Paying in advance with a bonus | Giving the builder a present
